  <Properties>
    <codeType>
      <Value><![CDATA[[
  "Design Code"
]]]></Value>
    </codeType>
    <description>
      <Value><![CDATA[{
  "blocks": {
    "contentData": [],
    "settingsData": [],
    "expose": [],
    "Layout": {}
  },
  "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EWhere larger-scale development is proposed adjacent to smaller-scale buildings, the design \u003Cstrong\u003Emust \u003C/strong\u003Eincorporate a gradual transition in height and massing (for example, by using a step-up approach in height and form) to: \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003Eminimise visual impact \u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003Eavoid abrupt or visually intrusive changes \u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003Eprevent overbearing or excessive shading \u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003Eensure sensitive integration with the existing built context, surrounding countryside, areas of open urban green space, and the setting of historic assets, particularly in relation to the skyline \u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EExceptions:\u003C/strong\u003E \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003Ecareful positioning of taller buildings \u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003Ecareful positioning of increased mass, scale, and height along blue networks, including canals and rivers\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C/p\u003E"
}]]></Value>
    </description>
